        "kind": "pull_request",
        "title": "fix: avoid model-not-found fallback on OpenRouter image-input 404s",
        "body": "Closes #99078\n\n## What Problem This Solves\n\nFixes an issue where users sending image input through an OpenRouter route could see missing-model fallback behavior when OpenRouter returned `HTTP 404: No endpoints found that support image input`. The model may exist; the rejected part is the image payload/capability, so treating it as `model_not_found` can produce misleading diagnostics and fallback decisions.\n\n## Why This Change Was Made\n\nThe failover classifier now recognizes image-input unsupported wording as a format/capability mismatch and preserves that classification through the HTTP 404 branch. Existing OpenRouter missing-model wording such as `No endpoints found for deepseek/deepseek-r1:free` still classifies as `model_not_found`.\n\n## User Impact\n\nOpenRouter image-capability rejections no longer masquerade as missing models. Users and operators get behavior aligned with the actual failure: the request included image input the selected route cannot accept, while real missing-model errors still trigger the existing model-not-found handling.\n\n## Evidence\n\nBefore fix proof:\n\n```text\nFAIL src/agents/failover-error.test.ts > failover-error > does not classify OpenRouter image-input no-endpoints 404s as model_not_found\nAssertionError: expected 'model_not_found' to be 'format'\n\nresolveFailoverReasonFromError({\n  status: 404,\n  message: \"No endpoints found that support image input\",\n})\n```\n\nAfter fix proof:\n\n```text\nnode scripts/run-vitest.mjs src/agents/live-model-errors.test.ts src/agents/failover-error.test.ts\n\nTest Files  2 passed (2)\nTests  95 passed (95)\n```\n\nAdditional checks:\n\n```text\npnpm exec oxlint src/agents/embedded-agent-helpers/errors.ts src/agents/live-model-errors.test.ts src/agents/failover-error.test.ts\ngit diff --check\npython .agents\\skills\\autoreview\\scripts\\autoreview --mode local\nautoreview clean: no accepted/actionable findings reported\n```\n",
        "branch": "fix/openrouter-image-input-error-classification",
